IO-13: report invalid cross-section geometry as ERROR 119 naming the link

6.0.0 copied legacy's ERROR 211 with an empty token for geometry that
setParams() refuses, and since 6.0.0 input errors carry no line number, the
message "ERROR 211: invalid number ." gives no way to find the link. Report
ERR_XSECT with the link name in both places (LinksHandler.cpp for Geom1 <= 0,
PostParseResolver.cpp for the rest), as the 5.3.0 patch does.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-13_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/input/PostParseResolver.cpp b/src/engine/input/PostParseResolver.cpp
index 807f527..f5868e1 100644
--- a/src/engine/input/PostParseResolver.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/input/PostParseResolver.cpp
@@ -3337,14 +3337,14 @@ void resolve_cross_references(SimulationContext& ctx) {
                     // setParams has answered "I cannot build a section from
                     // this" — the same verdict legacy's xsect_setParams returns
                     // as FALSE, and legacy refuses the deck on it
-                    // (link.c:250, ERROR 211 naming an empty token). v6 computed
+                    // (link.c:250, ERROR 119 naming the link). v6 computed
                     // the verdict and then threw it away, falling through to the
                     // rectangular fallback below: a MODBASKETHANDLE with a top
                     // width of 0, which has no geometry at all, ran as a
                     // rectangle. rc is what must be tested, not this branch —
                     // DUMMY reaches it with rc == 0, because setParams leaves a
                     // dummy's fields to the caller.
-                    ctx.errors.push_back(format_error(ERR_NUMBER, ""));
+                    ctx.errors.push_back(format_error(ERR_XSECT, ctx.link_names.name_of(j)));
                 }
                 // Invalid geometry — preserve the previous generic fallback.
                 a_full = w_max * y_full;
diff --git a/src/engine/input/handlers/LinksHandler.cpp b/src/engine/input/handlers/LinksHandler.cpp
index c205c9e..3593883 100644
--- a/src/engine/input/handlers/LinksHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/input/handlers/LinksHandler.cpp
@@ -432,14 +432,14 @@ void handle_xsections(SimulationContext& ctx, const std::vector<std::string>& li
             continue;
         }
         // Legacy xsect_setParams (xsect.c:233) refuses Geom1 <= 0 for every
-        // shape but DUMMY, and link.c:250 reports it as ERR_NUMBER with an
-        // empty token. (CUSTOM's own Geom1 test is link.c:226.)
+        // shape but DUMMY, and link.c:250 reports it as ERR_XSECT naming
+        // the link. (CUSTOM's own Geom1 test is link.c:226.)
         if (ctx.links.xsect_shape[idx] != XsectShape::IRREGULAR &&
             ctx.links.xsect_shape[idx] != XsectShape::STREET_XSECT &&
             ctx.links.xsect_shape[idx] != XsectShape::CUSTOM &&
             ctx.links.xsect_shape[idx] != XsectShape::DUMMY &&
             !(to_double(tok[2]) > 0.0)) {
-            ctx.errors.push_back(format_error(ERR_NUMBER, ""));
+            ctx.errors.push_back(format_error(ERR_XSECT, tok[0]));
             continue;
         }
 
